print(fibonacci(0))   # 0
print(fibonacci(1))   # 1
```

The `memo` dictionary caches computed values so each Fibonacci number is calculated only once, giving O(n) time and O(n) space complexity (instead of O(2ⁿ) time with naive recursion).
